# ============================================================
# .env.local.example — the NAMES a contributor needs, and nothing else.
#
# Copy this file to `.env.local` and fill in the values you were sent:
#
#     cp .env.local.example .env.local
#
# `.env.local` is gitignored. THIS file is not, and must never grow a real
# value — it exists so that the list of required names has ONE home that is
# checked in, instead of being retyped into a documentation page that then
# drifts from the code. `docs/start/install.md` points here.
#
# Placeholders are deliberately obvious. If a value below still looks like a
# placeholder when something fails, that is the bug.
# ============================================================

# ── RUN THE SITE — this is what almost everybody needs ────────────────────
#
# These two are the same pair the built website already carries in public: the
# address of the practice database and a visitor key that Postgres row-level
# security gates. Nothing here opens a door that a browser cannot already open.
#
# ⚠️ samo-dev is an UNMASKED COPY of production. Actions there are safe —
# nothing you click affects a real student. The DATA is not safe to publish:
# real names, real รหัสนักศึกษา, real photographs. Never publish the URL.
SUPABASE_DEV_URL=https://your-dev-project-ref.supabase.co
SUPABASE_DEV_ANON_KEY=paste-the-anon-key-here

# ── WORK ON THE DATABASE ITSELF — most people never need these ────────────
#
# ⛔ THESE TWO ARE NOT MORE OF THE SAME THING, and asking for "the full set"
# because it feels tidier is exactly the mistake this split exists to stop.
# They were handed out with the pair above until 2026-09-06, which meant every
# volunteer fixing a colour was carrying them on their laptop.
#
#   SUPABASE_DEV_ACCESS_TOKEN — can DELETE the whole samo-dev project.
#   SUPABASE_DEV_DB_URL       — a direct database login that IGNORES every
#                               permission rule: every real name, ID number and
#                               photograph in one connection.
#
# You need them only to run migrations (`npm run migrate:*`), the live proofs
# (`npm run proofs -- --dev`), `npm run dev:check` or `npm run dev:google`.
# Uncomment and fill in if you are doing that work; ask if you are not sure.
# SUPABASE_DEV_ACCESS_TOKEN=sbp_paste-the-management-token-here
# SUPABASE_DEV_DB_URL=postgresql://user:password@host:5432/postgres

# ── Optional: Google sign-in on previews (npm run dev:google) ──────────────
# Only needed if you are working on the sign-in flow itself. Dev-only client;
# it authenticates against samo-dev and nothing else.
# GOOGLE_DEV_CLIENT_ID=
# GOOGLE_DEV_CLIENT_SECRET=

# ── Optional: the Discord role sync, for local work ───────────────────────
#
# A SECOND Discord application, not the real one. Same tier as the two Google
# values above and shareable for the same reason: what it can do is bounded by
# what it was INVITED as, not by the code being careful.
#
# ⛔ Invite it with NO "Manage Roles". The sync's whole job is taking roles off
# people, so a dev bot that CAN write is a production credential wearing a dev
# label — and the report the local run produces needs nothing but the SERVER
# MEMBERS intent, which is a read. A permission you were never granted cannot
# be lost to a bug, a bad merge or a wrong `--apply` flag; a rule in the code
# saying "report only" can be lost to all three.
#
# ⛔ The REAL bot's token is not a variable in this file, commented or
# otherwise. It lives in the VM's systemd environment file and nowhere else —
# `/etc/samo-discord-bot.env`, root-owned, 0600. It has leaked into a chat
# transcript twice; a value that exists in two places leaks from the sloppier
# one. See `.claude/rules/security.md`.
# DISCORD_DEV_TOKEN=

# ── Maintainers only ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# These reach PRODUCTION. A contributor never needs them and should never be
# sent them. Listed by name so that a file containing them is recognisable,
# not so that anybody goes looking:
#   SUPABASE_ACCESS_TOKEN · SUPABASE_DB_URL · SAMO_VM_SUDO_PASSWORD
#   KKU_SSO_CLIENT_SECRET · GAS_SCRIPT_ID · GAS_DEPLOYMENT_ID
